{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Go now, see</b> — to say that he went out only with a good escort at the time he could see." "<b>and bring me back word</b> — a spark of ruach ha-kodesh flashed in him, that his end would be to return to him." "<b>עמק</b> in gematria is רד\"ו, for through this they were enslaved רד\"ו years. \"And he accompanied him to Hebron\" — his father said to him: Turn back. He said to him: It is written, \"Our hands did not shed this blood\" — that we did not send him off without escort, and thereby he would be exempt from us. And through this he remembered him, and that is what is written, \"and he saw the wagons that Joseph sent\" (Genesis 45:27). And this is what they said: A person should not take leave of his fellow except through words of Torah, for through this he remembers him."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:51.697833088Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}